          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectral+sequence"} spectral sequence
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/filtered+object"} filtered
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+complex"} chain complex
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mo ↪
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mo •
                  %mo ↪
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mi p
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mo •
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mo ↪
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mo •
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\cdots
                  \\hookrightarrow
                  F_{p-1}C_\bullet
                  \\hookrightarrow
                  F_p C_\bullet
                  \\hookrightarrow
                  \\cdots
                  \\hookrightarrow
                  C_\bullet
          %p
            is a tool for computing the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+homology"} chain homology
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mo •
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_\bullet
            from the chain homologies of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associated+graded+objects"} associated graded objects
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi G
                    %mi p
                  %mi C
                  %mo ≔
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mi p
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mo •
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ;
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  G_p C \coloneqq F_p C_\bullet/F_{p-1}C_\bullet
                  \\,;
          %p
            which is in general simpler. This is a special case of the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectral+sequence+of+a+filtered+stable+homotopy+type"} spectral sequence of a filtered stable homotopy type
          %p
            The sequence asymptotes to the homology of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mo •
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_\bullet
            by approximating
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cycles"} cycles
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/boundaries"} boundaries
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            by their “
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi r
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r
            \-approximation”: an
            %em
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi r
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r
              \-almost cycle
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain"} chain
            in filtering degree
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            whose
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential"} differential
            vanishes only up to terms that are
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi r
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r
            steps lower in filtering degree, and an
            = succeed "-almost" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi r
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            is a cycle that is the differential of a chain which may be (only) up to
            = succeed "-degrees" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi r
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r
            = succeed "-almost" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi r
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mo •
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_\bullet
            in filtering degree
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            is the term
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msubsup
                    %mi E
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo ,
                      %mo •
                    %mi r
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E^r_{p,\bullet}
            of the spectral sequence.
          %p
            If the filtering is bounded then
            = succeed "-almost" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi r
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi r
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r
            (“
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn ∞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            \-almost homology”) is clearly the genuine homology, and so the spectral sequence converges to the correct homology. But the point is that typically it reaches the correct value already at some low finite degree
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi r
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r
            (it “collapses”), and so allows one to obtain the genuine homology from some finite
            = succeed "-almost" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi r
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r
          %p
            One may also regard the spectral sequence of a filtered complex as a tool for organizing data derivable from the families of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/long+exact+sequence+in+homology"} long exact sequence in homology
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi H
                    %mi q
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi H
                    %mi q
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mi p
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi H
                    %mi q
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mi p
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mrow
                      %mi q
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi H
                    %mrow
                      %mi q
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mo •
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi ⋯
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\cdots
                  \\to
                  H_q (F_{p-1} C_\bullet)
                  \\to
                  H_q (F_p C_\bullet)
                  \\to
                  H_q(F_p C_\bullet / F_{q-1} C_\bullet)
                  \\to
                  H_{q-1}(F_{p-1} C_\bullet)
                  \\to
                  \\cdots
          %p which are induced by the short exact sequences
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 0
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mi q
                  %mo ↪
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mi p
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mi q
                  %mo →
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mi p
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mi q
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mi q
                  %mo →
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  0 \to F_{p-1}C_q \hookrightarrow F_p C_q \to F_p C_q / F_{p-1} C_q \to 0
          %p coming from the filtering.
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p We give the definition
          %ul
            %li
              %a{:href => "#ExplicitDefinition"} via relative homology
          %p and
          %ul
            %li
              %a{:href => "#ViaExactCouples"}> via exact couples
              \.
          %h3#ExplicitDefinition Via relative homology
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring"} ring
            and write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝒜
                  %mo =
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{A} = R
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mod"} Mod
            for its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modules"} modules
          %p Let
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mo ↪
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mo •
                  %mo ↪
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mi p
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mo •
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mo ↪
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mo •
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\cdots
                  \\hookrightarrow
                  F_{p-1}C_\bullet \hookrightarrow F_p C_\bullet \hookrightarrow
                  \\cdots
                  \\hookrightarrow
                  C_\bullet
          %p
            be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/filtered+chain+complex"} filtered chain complex
            in
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒜
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{A}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/associated+graded"} associated graded
            complex denoted
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi G
                      %mo •
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_\bullet C_\bullet
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p In more detail this means that
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ⋯
                        %mover
                          %mo →
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mo ∂
                              %mi n
                        %msub
                          %mi C
                          %mi n
                        %mover
                          %mo →
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mo ∂
                              %mrow
                                %mi n
                                %mo −
                                %mn 1
                        %msub
                          %mi C
                          %mrow
                            %mi n
                            %mo −
                            %mn 1
                        %mo →
                        %mi ⋯
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \cdots \stackrel{\partial_{n}}{\to} C_n \stackrel{\partial_{n-1}}{\to} C_{n-1} \to \cdots
                  is a
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+complex"} chain complex
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %msub
                          %mi C
                          %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{C_n\}
                  are
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
                  in
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝒜
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{A}
                  (
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi R
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
                  \-
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modules"}> modules
                  ) and
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %msub
                          %mo ∂
                          %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{\partial_n\}
                  are
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphisms"} morphisms
                  (module
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphisms"} homomorphisms
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mo ∂
                            %mi n
                          %mo ∘
                          %msub
                            %mo ∂
                            %mrow
                              %mi n
                              %mo +
                              %mn 1
                          %mo =
                          %mn 0
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \partial_n \circ \partial_{n+1} = 0
              %li
                %p
                  For each
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi ℤ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{Z}
                  there is a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/filtered+object"} filtering
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi F
                          %mo •
                        %msub
                          %mi C
                          %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_\bullet C_n
                  on
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi C
                          %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_n
                  and all these filterings are compatible with the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differentials"} differentials
                  in that
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo ∂
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi F
                          %mi p
                        %msub
                          %mi C
                          %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ⊂
                        %msub
                          %mi F
                          %mi p
                        %msub
                          %mi C
                          %mrow
                            %mi n
                            %mo −
                            %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        \\partial(F_p C_n) \subset F_p C_{n-1}
              %li
                %p
                  The grading associated to the filtering is such that the
                  = succeed "-graded" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi p
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient"} quotient
                .maruku-equation
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi G
                          %mi p
                        %msub
                          %mi C
                          %mi n
                        %mo ≔
                        %mfrac
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi F
                              %mi p
                            %msub
                              %mi C
                              %mi n
                          %mrow
                            %msub
                              %mi F
                              %mrow
                                %mi p
                                %mo −
                                %mn 1
                            %msub
                              %mi C
                              %mi n
                        %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                        %mo .
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                        G_p C_n \coloneqq \frac{F_p C_n}{ F_{p-1} C_n}
                        \\,.
                %p
                  Since the differentials respect the grading we have chain complexes
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi G
                          %mi p
                        %msub
                          %mi C
                          %mo •
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_p C_\bullet
                  in each filtering degree
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi p
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            %p
              The base category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒜
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{A}
              can be any abelian category. In this case, we still use element-notation as if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒜
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{A}
              were a category of
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modules"} modules
          %h4#InterpretationOfTerms
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi r
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r
            \-Almost cycles and boundaries
          #AlmostChainsCyclesBoundaries.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              Given a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/filtered+chain+complex"} filtered chain complex
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mo •
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_\bullet C_\bullet
              as above we say for all
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi r
                    %mo ,
                    %mi p
                    %mo ,
                    %mi q
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r, p, q \in \mathbb{Z}
              that
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi G
                          %mi p
                        %msub
                          %mi C
                          %mrow
                            %mi p
                            %mo +
                            %mi q
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G_p C_{p+q}
                  is the module of
                  %strong
                    %em
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                        %semantics
